---
// One patient's record, in the workspace (the Patients tab lit): a head
// of the facts that decide the next step — name, age, mobile, HMO, alerts,
// balance (finance roles), next and last visit, consent — then seven
// sections switched in place: Overview · Health · Chart · Visits · Money ·
// Consent · Texts (docs/workspace-redesign.md, "Patients"). The section is in
// the address (#health, #chart, …), so a reload, a post that comes back and
// a link all land on it. Money is shown only to people who may bill here
// (canBill in src/lib/invoices.ts), like the Finances tab.
//
// Drawn in the soft, very simple template (docs/workspace-redesign.md, "The
// soft template" and "Very simple"): the patient's avatar, name and a few facts
// with the chart no. as a small reference pill; one teal main action, New
// booking (the Dashboard's booking panel, the patient filled in), Edit details
// beside it and the rest under More (New charge, Bring in past visits); the
// alert chips; at most four numbers (next visit, last visit, balance, consent
// — the last two open their sections); the sections as one segmented control.
// The pages' own pieces are in ./_ui/ (patients.css, HealthLists, Callout,
// Head, Glyph).
//
// Every query runs inside withClinic(), so row-level security decides whether
// this patient exists here; a patient of another clinic (or a made-up id) is
// a 404 on reading and on every post. Opening the record writes
// patient.view to the audit log.
//
// The odontogram is src/components/Odontogram.astro, placed as it is: its
// offline logic (the kept copy of this page, changes waiting on the device)
// is untouched. A copy served offline opens on the Chart, and a notice the
// chart raises (a colleague's newer finding, changes waiting) brings the
// Chart forward.
//
// Four forms post back to this page, each with the CSRF token, checked before
// anything else (a miss comes back with ?stale=1):
//   intent=health   birth date, allergies, conditions, medicines, a note.
//                   saveHealth() in src/lib/health.ts: a new medical_history
//                   version under the person who saved it (a birth date
//                   change is kept in it, from and to), audit health.update /
//                   patient.birth_date. A save that started from an older
//                   version than the newest, or that changes a birth date
//                   someone else changed since, writes nothing and shows what
//                   the other person saved.
//   intent=consent  the privacy notice agreed at the desk (DeskConsent.astro),
//                   recordDeskConsent(): channel 'desk', who agreed (the
//                   patient, or a parent or guardian, named), audit
//                   consent.desk. Under 18 by the birth date on file, only a
//                   parent or guardian; with none on file, the desk says which.
//   intent=paper    a consent signed on paper (recordPaperConsent): a printed
//                   copy of the notice in force, dated on a day it was in
//                   force, or the clinic's own form (026). Audit consent.paper
//                   / consent.paper_form.
//   intent=details  Edit details (a side panel): name, chart no., sex, mobile,
//                   email, address, HMO, emergency contact, notes —
//                   updateDetails() in src/lib/import.ts, audit patient.update.
//                   The birth date stays with the health form, which keeps its
//                   history.
// All need staff_access.can_edit_records for this branch (every role has it
// today; see canEditRecords()). On success the page redirects to itself
// (?saved=…) so a reload does not post again; on a problem it renders again
// with what was typed.
//
// Patient forms (the QR code on the desk, src/lib/patient-forms.ts): a form
// added to this record comes here with ?saved=form&form=<id>, and the page
// says what it wrote (the consents as the record now has them: from the form,
// already on file, or none because the record makes the patient a minor who
// signed for themself; the allergies, conditions and medicines kept from the
// record), and lists each detail the form says differently, or a mobile or
// email the desk did not tick, with "Use <it>" (a fifth post, intent
// form-use: useFormDetail writes that one detail and comes back with
// &used=<field>). Names and the birth date are never offered. The page
// says what went on the record and, for a patient already on file, what the
// form says differently (kept as on file; Edit details changes it). The
// Overview shows what the latest form says about this visit (the reason, what
// is bothering them); Consent lists every form added here — when it was sent,
// who signed, the consents it wrote — with its answers and a printout
// (../forms/<id>/). A health version from a form reads "from the patient
// forms (QR-7K2F)".
export const prerender = false;

import ClinicLayout from '../../../../layouts/Clinic.astro';
import Csrf from '../../../../components/Csrf.astro';
import DeskConsent from '../../../../components/DeskConsent.astro';
import Odontogram from '../../../../components/Odontogram.astro';
import Pane from '../../../../components/ws/Pane.astro';
import Tile from '../../../../components/ws/Tile.astro';
import Chip from '../../../../components/ws/Chip.astro';
import Empty from '../../../../components/ws/Empty.astro';
import SidePanel from '../../../../components/ws/SidePanel.astro';
import Icon from '../../../../components/ws/Icon.astro';
import Avatar from '../../../../components/ws/Avatar.astro';
import Menu from '../../../../components/ws/Menu.astro';
import Head from './_ui/Head.astro';
import Callout from './_ui/Callout.astro';
import HealthLists from './_ui/HealthLists.astro';
import Glyph from './_ui/Glyph.astro';
import './_ui/patients.css';
import './_forms/forms.css';
import './_record/record.css';
import Timeline from './_record/Timeline.astro';
import Treatment from './_record/Treatment.astro';
import Notes from './_record/Notes.astro';
import Prescriptions from './_record/Prescriptions.astro';
import Files from './_record/Files.astro';
import RecallCard from './_record/RecallCard.astro';
import Vitals from './_record/Vitals.astro';
import Letters from './_record/Letters.astro';
import Loas from './_record/Loas.astro';
import PayPlans from './_record/PayPlans.astro';
import RecordNav from './_record/RecordNav.astro';
import Banner from './_record/Banner.astro';
import { shellLinks } from '../../../../components/ws/routes';
import { requireWorkspace } from '../../../../lib/workspace';
import { withClinic } from '../../../../lib/db';
import { csrfOk, csrfToken, CSRF_MESSAGE } from '../../../../lib/csrf';
import { hit, waitText, LIMITS } from '../../../../lib/throttle';
import {
  LISTS, NOTE_MAX, NAME_MAX, manilaToday, ageOn, ageText, when, day, oneLine, readHealthForm, saveHealth, readHealth,
  canEditRecords, readConsents, noticeInForce, recordDeskConsent, versionChanges, listText, answered, dateText, capitalise,
  consentInForce, readPaperForms, readPaperForm, recordPaperConsent, PAPER_WORDS,
  type HealthAnswers, type HealthVersion, type AgreedAs, type PaperIn,
} from '../../../../lib/health';
import { readPersonForm, updateDetails, hmoSuggestions, SEXES, NOTES_MAX, type PersonIn } from '../../../../lib/import';
import { pesos, statementNo, STATUS as BILL_STATUS, fromDb } from '../../../../lib/invoices';
import { prettyPhone } from '../../../../lib/messages';
import { hmos } from '../../../../data/directory';
import { CONDITION_LABEL, surfaceSummary, type ToothCondition, type ToothMark, type Surface, type Notation } from '../../../../data/demo';
import { patientForms, getForm, compareWithRecord, useFormDetail, healthLists, answerText, FIELDS, TAKEABLE, type FormConsentState } from '../../../../lib/patient-forms';
import { signedText } from './_forms/words';
import { can } from '../../../../lib/can';
import { loadClinical, loadTimeline, recordAction, RECORD_INTENTS, RX_ROWS, type Outcome, type RecordProblem, type RxItem } from '../../../../lib/record';
import { loadExtra, extraAction, extraEvents, bpWords, EXTRA_INTENTS, EXTRA_ANCHOR } from '../../../../lib/record-extra';

const ws = await requireWorkspace(Astro);
if (ws instanceof Response) return ws;
const { clinic, session, branches } = ws;
const money = can(clinic, 'finance.bill');
const links = shellLinks(clinic.slug);

const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;
const patientId = Astro.params.patient ?? '';
const notFound = () => new Response('No such patient', { status: 404 });
if (!UUID.test(patientId)) return notFound();
const here = `/c/${clinic.slug}/patients/${patientId}/`;
const HMO_NAMES = new Map(hmos.map((h) => [h.id, h.name]));
const q = Astro.url.searchParams;

// What a post left behind for the page to show.
let healthProblems: string[] = [];
let posted: { answers: HealthAnswers; birth: string; birthWas: string; base: string } | null = null;
let conflict: { latest: HealthVersion | null; birth: string | null; versionMoved: boolean; birthMoved: boolean } | null = null;
let consentProblem: string | null = null;
let givenBy = '';
let agreedAs: AgreedAs | null = null;
let paperState: { open: boolean; problem: string | null; values: Partial<PaperIn> } = { open: false, problem: null, values: {} };
let detailsProblems: string[] = [];
let detailsPosted: PersonIn | null = null;
let formUseProblem: string | null = null;
// A clinical-record post (Treatment, Notes, Prescriptions, Files, the next check-up) that was refused.
let recordProblem: RecordProblem | null = null;
let rxTyped: RxItem[] = [];
// The section a post came back to.
let backTo: string | null = null;
// Where on the page a clinical-record post lands again.
const ANCHOR: Record<string, string> = { 'done-add': 'treatment-done', 'lab-add': 'treatment-lab', 'lab-next': 'treatment-lab', 'recall-set': 'recall', 'recall-done': 'recall', 'recall-clear': 'recall' };
/** A refused clinical-record post: thrown out of the transaction so nothing half-done is kept. */
class Refused extends Error { constructor(public outcome: Extract<Outcome, { ok: false }>) { super('refused'); } }

if (Astro.request.method === 'POST') {
  const form = await Astro.request.formData();
  if (!csrfOk(Astro.cookies, form)) return Astro.redirect(here + '?stale=1', 303);
  const intent = String(form.get('intent') ?? '');
  // Same allowance as the chart: a person saving never meets it; a script does.
  const rate = await hit('record:s:' + session.staffId, ...LIMITS.chart.staff);
  const slow = rate.allowed ? null : 'Too many saves at once. ' + waitText(rate.retryAfter);

  if (intent === 'health') {
    backTo = 'health';
    const { answers, birth, problems } = readHealthForm(form);
    let base = String(form.get('base') ?? '');
    // The birth date this page opened with: a save changes the birth date only when this person changed it.
    let birthWas = oneLine(form.get('birth_was'));
    let birthShown = oneLine(form.get('birth_date'));
    if (slow) problems.unshift(slow);
    if (problems.length === 0) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? saveHealth(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, base, answers, birth, birthWas: birthWas || null })
          : ({ kind: 'denied' } as const));
      if (r.kind === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r.kind === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=${r.answers ? 'health' : 'birth'}#health`, 303);
      if (r.kind === 'unchanged') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=nothing#health`, 303);
      if (r.kind === 'denied') problems.push('Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.');
      if (r.kind === 'conflict') {
        conflict = { latest: r.latest, birth: r.birth, versionMoved: (r.latest?.id ?? 'none') !== base, birthMoved: (r.birth ?? '') !== birthWas };
        // The next Save starts from what is on file now. A birth date this person
        // did not change shows the one on file; one they changed stays as typed.
        if (birthShown === birthWas) birthShown = r.birth ?? '';
        base = r.latest?.id ?? 'none';
        birthWas = r.birth ?? '';
      }
    }
    healthProblems = problems;
    posted = { answers, birth: birthShown, birthWas, base };
  } else if (intent === 'consent') {
    backTo = 'consent';
    givenBy = oneLine(form.get('given_by_name'));
    const who = String(form.get('agreed_as') ?? '');
    agreedAs = who === 'patient' || who === 'guardian' ? who : null;
    if (slow) consentProblem = slow;
    else if (form.get('agreed') !== '1') consentProblem = 'Tick the box that says they agreed, once they have. Nothing was recorded.';
    else if (givenBy.length > NAME_MAX) consentProblem = `Keep the name under ${NAME_MAX} characters.`;
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? recordDeskConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, version: String(form.get('version') ?? ''), givenBy: givenBy || null, agreedAs })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent#consent`, 303);
      if (r === 'already') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent-already#consent`, 303);
      consentProblem = {
        denied: 'Your account cannot record consent at this branch. Ask the owner.',
        who: 'Choose who is agreeing: the patient, 18 or over, or a parent or guardian. Nothing was recorded.',
        minor: 'The birth date on file makes the patient under 18, so a parent or guardian agrees for them. Ask them to type their name. Nothing was recorded.',
        'guardian-name': 'A parent or guardian is agreeing, so they type their name. Nothing was recorded.',
        'no-notice': 'No privacy notice is in force, so there is nothing to record.',
        changed: 'The privacy notice changed while this page was open. Show the patient the new one below.',
      }[r];
      if (r === 'minor') agreedAs = 'guardian';
    }
  } else if (intent === 'paper') {
    backTo = 'consent';
    const { paper, problems } = readPaperForm(form);
    paperState = { open: true, problem: slow ?? (problems.length ? problems.join(' ') : null), values: paper };
    if (!paperState.problem) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? recordPaperConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, ...paper })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=paper#consent-paper`, 303);
      paperState.problem = r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot record consent at this branch. Ask the owner.' : `${PAPER_WORDS[r]} Nothing was recorded.`;
    }
  } else if (intent === 'details') {
    backTo = 'overview';
    const { person, problems } = readPersonForm(form);
    detailsPosted = person;
    if (slow) problems.unshift(slow);
    if (!problems.length) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? updateDetails(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, p: person })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=details#overview`, 303);
      problems.push(r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.' : r.taken);
    }
    detailsProblems = problems;
  } else if (RECORD_INTENTS.has(intent) || EXTRA_INTENTS.has(intent)) {
    // The clinical record (src/lib/record.ts): every intent checks canEditRecords in its own transaction.
    const outcome = slow
      ? ({ ok: false, section: 'overview', problem: slow, values: {} } as Extract<Outcome, { ok: false }>)
      : await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
          const o = EXTRA_INTENTS.has(intent)
            ? await extraAction(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, canBill: money, hmoNames: HMO_NAMES }, intent, form)
            : await recordAction(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId }, intent, form);
          if (o !== 'none' && !o.ok) throw new Refused(o);
          return o;
        }).catch((e) => { if (e instanceof Refused) return e.outcome; throw e; });
    if (outcome === 'none') return notFound();
    if (outcome.ok) return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=${encodeURIComponent(outcome.saved)}#${ANCHOR[intent] ?? EXTRA_ANCHOR[intent] ?? outcome.section}`, 303);
    backTo = slow ? null : outcome.section;
    recordProblem = { intent, text: outcome.problem, values: outcome.values };
    if (intent === 'rx-add') {
      const col = (k: string) => form.getAll(k).map((x) => String(x));
      const [dr, st, qt, sg] = [col('drug'), col('strength'), col('qty'), col('sig')];
      rxTyped = Array.from({ length: RX_ROWS }, (_, i) => ({ drug: dr[i] ?? '', strength: st[i] ?? '', qty: qt[i] ?? '', sig: sg[i] ?? '' }));
    }
  } else if (intent === 'form-use') {
    // One detail from an added patient form onto the record ("Use 0917 555 0199").
    backTo = 'overview';
    const formId = String(form.get('form') ?? '');
    const field = String(form.get('field') ?? '');
    if (slow) formUseProblem = slow;
    else if (!UUID.test(formId) || !TAKEABLE.has(field)) formUseProblem = 'That detail cannot be taken from the form. Nothing was changed.';
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, (tx) => useFormDetail(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, formId, field }));
      if (r === 'saved' || r === 'same') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?form=${formId}&used=${encodeURIComponent(field)}#overview`, 303);
      formUseProblem = r === 'not-allowed' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.' : 'That form is not on this record any more. Nothing was changed.';
    }
  }
}

const data = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
  const me = (await tx.query('select area, notation from clinic where id = $1', [clinic.id])).rows[0];
  const p = (await tx.query(
    `select p.id, p.chart_no, p.first_name, p.middle_name, p.last_name, p.suffix, p.sex, p.phone, p.email::text as email,
            p.address_line, p.city, p.province, p.hmo_name, p.hmo_member_no, p.emergency_name, p.emergency_relation, p.emergency_phone, p.notes,
            to_char(p.birth_date, 'YYYY-MM-DD') as birth, p.created_at, p.import_id is not null as imported, cs.full_name as created_by_name,
            patient_balance(p.id) as balance
       from patient p left join staff cs on cs.id = p.created_by
      where p.id = $1 and p.archived_at is null`, [patientId])).rows[0];
  if (!p) return null;
  const teeth = (await tx.query(`select fdi, surface, condition from tooth_state where patient_id = $1 and superseded_at is null order by fdi`, [p.id])).rows;
  const visits = (await tx.query(
    `select a.id, a.starts_at, a.reason, a.status, a.source, a.date_only, a.teeth, a.notes, a.chair,
            coalesce(s.full_name, a.dentist_name) as dentist, a.dentist_name is not null as dentist_free,
            (select i.total from invoice i where i.appointment_id = a.id and i.status <> 'void' order by i.issued_at limit 1) as charged
       from appointment a left join staff s on s.id = a.dentist_id
      where a.patient_id = $1 order by a.starts_at desc limit 200`, [p.id])).rows;
  const next = (await tx.query(
    `select a.starts_at, a.reason, a.status, s.full_name as dentist from appointment a left join staff s on s.id = a.dentist_id
      where a.patient_id = $1 and a.status not in ('cancelled', 'no_show', 'completed')
        and (a.starts_at >= now() - interval '1 hour' or a.status in ('arrived', 'in_lobby', 'in_chair'))
      order by a.status in ('arrived', 'in_lobby', 'in_chair') desc, a.starts_at limit 1`, [p.id])).rows[0] ?? null;
  // Who looked. Required to answer a subject-access request.
  await tx.query(`insert into audit_log (clinic_id, staff_id, action, entity, entity_id) values ($1, $2, 'patient.view', 'patient', $3)`, [clinic.id, session.staffId, p.id]);
  const health = await readHealth(tx, p.id);
  const consents = await readConsents(tx, p.id);
  const paperForms = await readPaperForms(tx, p.id);
  const notice = await noticeInForce(tx);
  const canEdit = await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id);
  // clinic_group has no tenant; the group id came from requireWorkspace().
  const dpo = (await tx.query('select dpo_name from clinic_group where id = $1', [clinic.group_id])).rows[0]?.dpo_name ?? null;
  const statements = money ? (await tx.query(
    `select i.id, i.series_prefix, i.number, i.issued_at, i.status, i.total, i.payor_name, i.payor_share, i.imported_at, coalesce(y.paid, 0) as paid,
            (select l.description from invoice_line l where l.invoice_id = i.id order by l.line_no nulls last, l.id limit 1) as first_line,
            (select count(*)::int from invoice_line l where l.invoice_id = i.id) as n_lines
       from invoice i left join lateral (select sum(amount) as paid from payment where invoice_id = i.id and voided_at is null) y on true
      where i.patient_id = $1 and i.status <> 'draft' order by i.issued_at desc, i.number desc limit 100`, [p.id])).rows : [];
  // Texts about this patient. A sign-in code is never one of them, and its body is never read (CLAUDE.md, Backend).
  const texts = (await tx.query(
    `select m.id, m.direction, m.kind, m.status, m.created_at, m.sent_at, m.failed_reason,
            case when m.kind in ('reset', 'invite') then null else m.body end as body
       from message_log m where m.patient_id = $1 and m.channel = 'sms' order by m.created_at desc limit 50`, [p.id])).rows;
  const hmoNames = canEdit ? await hmoSuggestions(tx, new Map(hmos.map((h) => [h.id, h.name]))) : [];
  // The patient forms added to this record, the newest one's answers (this visit's reason), and — just after
  // "Add to <patient>" — what that form says differently from the record now.
  const forms = await patientForms(tx, p.id);
  const latestForm = forms[0] ? await getForm(tx, forms[0].id) : null;
  // Just after a form was added (?saved=form), or one of its details used (?used=): that form.
  const addedId = q.get('saved') === 'form' || q.has('used') || formUseProblem ? q.get('form') ?? '' : '';
  const addedLine = addedId && UUID.test(addedId) ? forms.find((f) => f.id === addedId) ?? null : null;
  const added = addedLine ? await getForm(tx, addedLine.id) : null;
  // What the form says that the record does not: different, or a mobile or email the desk did not take.
  const cmp = added && added.addedAs === 'existing' ? await compareWithRecord(tx, added.values, p.id) : null;
  const addedDiffers = cmp ? [...cmp.differs, ...cmp.proposed] : [];
  // The clinical record (033) and the Timeline, which reads everything above once more in one list.
  const clinical = await loadClinical(tx, clinic.id, p.id);
  const extra = await loadExtra(tx, p.id, HMO_NAMES);
  const timeline = [...(await loadTimeline(tx, p.id, clinical, money)), ...extraEvents(extra, money)].sort((a, b) => +new Date(b.at) - +new Date(a.at));
  return { clinical, extra, timeline, me, p, teeth, visits, next, health, consents, paperForms, notice, canEdit, dpo: dpo as string | null, statements, texts, hmoNames, forms, latestForm, added, addedLine, addedDiffers };
});
if (!data) return notFound();
const { me, p: patient, visits, health, canEdit } = data;

// Rows per (tooth, surface) become one mark per tooth for the chart. The chart
// keeps one biting-surface slot and names it incisal on anteriors itself, so an
// 'incisal' row lands in that slot.
const marks: Partial<Record<number, ToothMark>> = {};
for (const t of data.teeth) {
  const m = (marks[t.fdi] ??= { condition: t.condition as ToothCondition });
  if (!t.surface) continue;
  const surface = (t.surface === 'incisal' ? 'occlusal' : t.surface) as Surface;
  if (!(m.surfaces ??= []).includes(surface)) m.surfaces.push(surface);
}

// The chart posts each change to /api/chart with this token in the X-CSRF header.
const csrf = csrfToken(Astro.cookies);

const today = manilaToday();
const age = patient.birth ? ageOn(patient.birth, today) : null;
const minor = age !== null && age < 18;
// The consent that counts for the notice in force, and whether a minor still needs a parent's or guardian's.
const consentNow = consentInForce(data.notice?.id, data.consents);
const guardianNeeded = minor && consentNow?.agreed_as !== 'guardian';
const latest = health.versions[0] ?? null;
// The alert strip is what is saved; the form shows what was typed when a post came back.
const allergies: string[] = latest?.allergies ?? [];
const conditions: string[] = latest?.conditions ?? [];
const medications: string[] = latest?.medications ?? [];
const shown: HealthAnswers = posted?.answers ?? { allergies: latest?.allergies ?? null, conditions: latest?.conditions ?? null, medications: latest?.medications ?? null, note: latest?.note ?? null };
const birthValue = posted ? posted.birth : patient.birth ?? '';
const birthWas = posted ? posted.birthWas : patient.birth ?? '';
const formAge = birthValue ? ageOn(birthValue, today) : null;
const base = posted?.base ?? latest?.id ?? 'none';
const saved = q.get('saved');
const stale = q.get('stale') === '1';

// Existing findings, newest concern first so the dentist reads problems before completed work.
const ORDER: ToothCondition[] = ['caries', 'missing', 'impacted', 'unerupted', 'root_canal', 'crown', 'bridge', 'implant', 'veneer', 'filled', 'sealant', 'sound'];
const findings = Object.entries(marks)
  .map(([fdi, m]) => ({ fdi: Number(fdi), condition: m!.condition, codes: surfaceSummary(Number(fdi), m!.surfaces) }))
  .sort((a, b) => ORDER.indexOf(a.condition) - ORDER.indexOf(b.condition) || a.fdi - b.fdi);

// The same way every date on the record reads: "Fri 25 Sep 2026, 9:00 am".
const visitWhen = (d: Date) => when(d);
const manilaDay = (d: Date) => new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-CA', { timeZone: 'Asia/Manila', year: 'numeric', month: '2-digit', day: '2-digit' }).format(d);
/** A visit's day and time, or its day alone when only the day is known (brought in from old records). */
const visitText = (v: { starts_at: Date; date_only: boolean }) => (v.date_only ? dateText(manilaDay(v.starts_at))! : visitWhen(v.starts_at));
const SOURCE: Record<string, string> = { web: 'Web', request: 'Web request', staff: 'Desk', import: 'Imported' };

// The chips: the quick picks in a fixed order (the same place every time), then
// anything else on the record or typed, ticked.
const lower = (s: string) => s.toLocaleLowerCase('en');
const chipsFor = (key: (typeof LISTS)[number]['key'], picks: readonly string[]) => {
  const on = shown[key] ?? [];
  const extra = on.filter((v) => !picks.some((p) => lower(p) === lower(v)));
  return [...picks, ...extra].map((v) => ({ value: v, on: on.some((x) => lower(x) === lower(v)) }));
};
const healthChips = Object.fromEntries(LISTS.map((l) => [l.key, chipsFor(l.key, l.picks)]));
const healthNone = Object.fromEntries(LISTS.map((l) => [l.key, shown[l.key]?.length === 0]));

// A version from the patient forms is dated when it went on the record; the line says when it was sent.
const byLine = (v: HealthVersion) =>
  `${when(new Date(v.at))}${v.by ? ` by ${v.by}` : v.answeredBy === 'patient'
    ? ` from the patient forms${v.formRef ? ` (${v.formRef}${v.formSentAt ? `, sent ${day(new Date(v.formSentAt))}` : ''})` : ''}` : ''}`;
const stateLine = (v: HealthAnswers) =>
  [...LISTS.map((l) => `${l.label} ${listText(v[l.key], l.key === 'allergies' ? 'none known' : 'none')}`), v.note && `Note: ${v.note}`].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');
const birthLine = (b: string | null) => `Birth date ${dateText(b) ?? 'not on file'}`;
/** A list as one plain line: "Penicillin, Latex", "None known", "Not asked yet". */
const listLine = (v: string[] | null, none: string) => (v === null ? 'Not asked yet' : capitalise(listText(v, none)));

// --- the head ---------------------------------------------------------------
const fullName = [patient.first_name, patient.middle_name, patient.last_name, patient.suffix].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
const shortName = `${patient.first_name} ${patient.last_name}`;
const titleName = patient.suffix ? `${shortName} ${patient.suffix}` : shortName;
const SEX: Record<string, string> = { female: 'Female', male: 'Male', other: 'Other', undisclosed: 'Sex not said' };
// Under the name: the few facts the desk reads out. The chart no. sits beside them as a small reference pill.
const facts = [
  age !== null ? ageText(age) : null,
  patient.sex ? SEX[patient.sex] : null,
  patient.phone ? prettyPhone(patient.phone) : null,
  patient.hmo_name ? patient.hmo_name : null,
].filter(Boolean) as string[];
const balance = fromDb(patient.balance);
const lastVisit = visits.find((v) => v.status === 'completed') ?? null;
const nextVisit = data.next;
const nextParts = (d: Date) => new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { weekday: 'short', day: 'numeric', month: 'short', hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit', timeZone: 'Asia/Manila' }).formatToParts(d).reduce((o, x) => ({ ...o, [x.type]: x.value }), {} as Record<string, string>);
// A visit under way (arrived, waiting, in the chair) is the one that matters now.
const HERE: Record<string, string> = { arrived: 'Arrived', in_lobby: 'Waiting', in_chair: 'In the chair' };
const hereNow = nextVisit ? HERE[nextVisit.status] ?? null : null;
const nextValue = hereNow ?? (nextVisit ? (() => { const x = nextParts(nextVisit.starts_at); return `${x.weekday} ${x.day} ${x.month}`; })() : 'None');
const nextNote = nextVisit ? (() => { const x = nextParts(nextVisit.starts_at); return [`${x.hour}:${x.minute} ${String(x.dayPeriod).toLowerCase()}`, nextVisit.reason, nextVisit.dentist].filter(Boolean).join(' · '); })() : 'Nothing on the calendar yet';
const consentValue = !data.notice ? '—' : consentNow && !guardianNeeded ? 'On record' : guardianNeeded && consentNow ? 'Guardian needed' : 'Not yet';
const consentNote = !data.notice ? 'No notice in force'
  : consentNow && !guardianNeeded ? (consentNow.channel === 'paper' && consentNow.signed_on ? `Signed on paper ${dateText(consentNow.signed_on)}` : `Given ${day(new Date(consentNow.given_at))}`)
  : data.paperForms.length ? 'Clinic’s own form on file; ask for the notice' : 'Ask at the desk';
const bookHref = `${links.newBooking}&patient=${patient.id}`;
const chargeHref = `${links.newCharge}?patient=${patient.id}`;
const importHref = `/c/${clinic.slug}/patients/import/`;

// --- sections ---------------------------------------------------------------
const clin = data.clinical;
const ext = data.extra;
// The head's safety chips (034): the latest blood pressure when it was taken today or is out of range, and
// whether a physician's clearance is needed (a high reading in the last 30 days with no clearance since, a
// request still waiting, or a physician who did not clear) — always words, never colour alone.
const latestBp = ext.vitals.find((x) => x.sys && x.dia) ?? null;
const bpNow = latestBp ? bpWords(latestBp.sys!, latestBp.dia!) : null;
const bpDay = latestBp ? manilaDay(new Date(latestBp.at)) : null;
const bpRecent = !!latestBp && Date.now() - +new Date(latestBp.at) < 30 * 864e5;
const bpChip = latestBp && bpNow && (bpDay === today || (bpRecent && bpNow.tone !== 'neutral'))
  ? { text: `BP ${latestBp.sys}/${latestBp.dia}${bpDay === today ? ' today' : ` on ${dateText(bpDay)}`}${bpNow.tone !== 'neutral' ? ` · ${bpNow.label.toLowerCase()}` : ''}`, tone: bpNow.tone } : null;
const lastClearance = ext.letters.find((l) => l.kind === 'clearance') ?? null;
const clearedSince = !!lastClearance?.answer && lastClearance.answer !== 'not_cleared' && !!bpDay && (lastClearance.answeredOn ?? '') >= bpDay;
const clearance: { text: string; tone: 'alert' | 'warn' | 'accent' } | null =
  lastClearance && !lastClearance.answer ? { text: 'Waiting for medical clearance', tone: 'warn' }
  : lastClearance?.answer === 'not_cleared' ? { text: 'Physician has not cleared treatment', tone: 'alert' }
  : bpRecent && (bpNow?.level === 'high' || bpNow?.level === 'crisis') && !clearedSince ? { text: 'Needs medical clearance', tone: 'alert' }
  : lastClearance?.answer && lastClearance.answeredOn && Date.now() - Date.parse(`${lastClearance.answeredOn}T00:00:00+08:00`) < 180 * 864e5 ? { text: `Cleared by physician ${dateText(lastClearance.answeredOn)}`, tone: 'accent' }
  : null;
const behindPlans = money ? ext.plans.filter((x) => x.status === 'active' && x.missed > 0) : [];
const loaWaiting = ext.loas.filter((a) => a.status === 'requested').length;
const planOpen = clin.plan.filter((i) => i.status === 'planned' || i.status === 'accepted');
const SECTIONS = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'timeline', label: 'Timeline' },
  { id: 'health', label: 'Health' },
  { id: 'chart', label: 'Chart' },
  { id: 'treatment', label: 'Treatment', count: planOpen.length || null },
  { id: 'notes', label: 'Notes', count: clin.notes.filter((n) => !n.amends).length || null },
  { id: 'rx', label: 'Rx & letters', count: (clin.rx.length + ext.letters.length) || null },
  { id: 'files', label: 'Files', count: clin.files.length || null },
  { id: 'visits', label: 'Visits', count: visits.length || null },
  ...(money ? [{ id: 'money', label: 'Money', count: data.statements.filter((s) => s.status === 'issued' || s.status === 'partly_paid').length || null }] : []),
  { id: 'consent', label: 'Consent' },
  { id: 'texts', label: 'Texts', count: data.texts.length || null },
];
const savedTo: Record<string, string> = { health: 'health', birth: 'health', nothing: 'health', consent: 'consent', 'consent-already': 'consent', paper: 'consent', details: 'overview', new: 'overview', form: 'overview' };

// --- a patient form just added ------------------------------------------------
// The consents as the record has them now, in words (never a claim the rows do not make).
const CONSENT_KIND: Record<'privacy' | 'treatment', string> = { privacy: 'the privacy notice', treatment: 'the consent to examination and treatment' };
const consentWords = (st: { privacy: FormConsentState; treatment: FormConsentState }) => {
  const from = (['treatment', 'privacy'] as const).filter((k) => st[k] === 'form').map((k) => CONSENT_KIND[k]);
  const onFile = (['treatment', 'privacy'] as const).filter((k) => st[k] === 'on-file').map((k) => CONSENT_KIND[k]);
  const none = (['treatment', 'privacy'] as const).filter((k) => st[k] === 'none');
  return { from, onFile, none };
};
const addedConsents = data.addedLine ? consentWords(data.addedLine.consentState) : null;
const andList = (xs: string[]) => (xs.length <= 1 ? xs.join('') : `${xs.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and ${xs[xs.length - 1]}`);
// What the new health version kept from the record that the form did not say (Add to <patient>).
const lowerEq = (a: string, b: string) => a.toLocaleLowerCase('en') === b.toLocaleLowerCase('en');
const keptFromRecord = (() => {
  if (!data.added || data.added.addedAs !== 'existing') return [] as string[];
  const v = health.versions.find((x) => x.formRef === data.added!.ref);
  if (!v) return [];
  const fromForm = healthLists(data.added.values);
  return (['allergies', 'conditions', 'medications'] as const).flatMap((k) => (v[k] ?? []).filter((x) => !fromForm[k].some((y) => lowerEq(x, y))));
})();
const used = q.get('used');
const usedLabel = used ? ({ phone: 'mobile', email: 'email', address_line: 'address', city: 'city', province: 'province', sex: 'sex', occupation: 'occupation',
  emergency_name: 'emergency contact', emergency_relation: 'emergency contact’s relation', emergency_phone: 'emergency contact’s number',
  guardian_name: 'parent or guardian', guardian_relation: 'parent or guardian’s relation', guardian_phone: 'parent or guardian’s mobile',
  hmo_name: 'HMO', hmo_member_no: 'HMO card number', middle_name: 'middle name', suffix: 'suffix' } as Record<string, string>)[used] ?? 'detail' : null;
// A clinical-record save names its section by its first word (plan-done, rx:<id>, files:3, recall-cleared …).
const recordSaved = (s: string | null) => {
  const w = (s ?? '').split(/[-:]/)[0];
  return ({ plan: 'treatment', done: 'treatment', lab: 'treatment', note: 'notes', addendum: 'notes', rx: 'rx', file: 'files', files: 'files', recall: 'overview',
    vitals: 'health', letter: 'rx', answered: 'rx', loa: 'treatment', payplan: 'treatment', adjusted: 'treatment' } as Record<string, string>)[w] ?? null;
};
const current = backTo ?? savedTo[saved ?? ''] ?? recordSaved(saved) ?? 'overview';
const SECTION_LABEL = Object.fromEntries(SECTIONS.map((x) => [x.id, x.label])) as Record<string, string>;

// --- money --------------------------------------------------------------------
const stmts = data.statements.map((s) => {
  const total = fromDb(s.total), paid = fromDb(s.paid);
  return { ...s, total, paid, left: s.status === 'void' ? 0n : total - paid };
});
const paidAll = stmts.filter((s) => s.status !== 'void').reduce((n, s) => n + s.paid, 0n);
const openCount = stmts.filter((s) => s.status === 'issued' || s.status === 'partly_paid').length;
// A statement's status as a soft pill: paid is green (money in), unpaid red, part-paid amber, void quiet.
const STMT_TINT: Record<string, string> = { paid: 'ws-tint-green', issued: 'ws-tint-red', partly_paid: 'ws-tint-amber' };

// --- texts ---------------------------------------------------------------------
const TEXT_KIND: Record<string, string> = { confirmation: 'Booking confirmation', reminder: 'Reminder', manual: 'Note', reply: 'Reply' };
const textStatus = (m: { direction: string; status: string }) =>
  m.direction === 'in' ? { label: 'Received', tone: 'accent' as const }
  : m.status === 'failed' ? { label: 'Failed', tone: 'alert' as const }
  : m.status === 'delivered' ? { label: 'Delivered', tone: 'accent' as const }
  : m.status === 'sent' ? { label: 'Sent', tone: 'muted' as const }
  : m.status === 'cancelled' ? { label: 'Cancelled', tone: 'muted' as const }
  : { label: 'Waiting to send', tone: 'neutral' as const };

// --- details -------------------------------------------------------------------
const d = detailsPosted ?? {
  chartNo: patient.chart_no, first: patient.first_name, middle: patient.middle_name, last: patient.last_name, suffix: patient.suffix, sex: patient.sex,
  phone: patient.phone, email: patient.email, address: patient.address_line, city: patient.city, province: patient.province, hmoName: patient.hmo_name,
  hmoMemberNo: patient.hmo_member_no, emergencyName: patient.emergency_name, emergencyRelation: patient.emergency_relation, emergencyPhone: patient.emergency_phone, notes: patient.notes,
};
const address = [patient.address_line, patient.city, patient.province].filter(Boolean).join(', ');
const detailRows: [string, string | null][] = [
  ['Full name', fullName],
  ['Birth date', patient.birth ? `${dateText(patient.birth)}${age !== null ? ` · ${ageText(age)}` : ''}` : null],
  ['Sex', patient.sex ? SEX[patient.sex] : null],
  ['Mobile', patient.phone ? prettyPhone(patient.phone) : null],
  ['Email', patient.email],
  ['Address', address || null],
  ['HMO', patient.hmo_name ? `${patient.hmo_name}${patient.hmo_member_no ? ` · member no. ${patient.hmo_member_no}` : ''}` : null],
  ['Emergency contact', patient.emergency_name ? [patient.emergency_name, patient.emergency_relation, patient.emergency_phone && prettyPhone(patient.emergency_phone)].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') : null],
  ['Chart no.', patient.chart_no],
  ['On file since', `${dateText(manilaDay(patient.created_at))}${patient.imported ? ', from an import' : patient.created_by_name ? `, added by ${patient.created_by_name}` : ''}`],
];
// Only what is on file is listed; what is missing is one line, with the way to add it.
const present = detailRows.filter(([, v]) => v);
const missing = detailRows.filter(([, v]) => !v).map(([k]) => (k === 'HMO' ? k : k.toLowerCase()));
const help = 'text-[13px] leading-snug text-muted';
// The latest patient form's words about this visit, for the Overview.
const lf = data.latestForm?.values ?? null;
const visitFromForm: [string, string][] = lf ? ([
  ['Reason for the visit', lf.reason],
  ['Bothering them', answerText(FIELDS.concerns, lf.concerns) ? [answerText(FIELDS.concerns, lf.concerns), lf.concern_other].filter(Boolean).join(', ') : null],
  ['Last dental visit', answerText(FIELDS.last_visit, lf.last_visit)],
  ['Nervous about visits', answerText(FIELDS.nervous, lf.nervous)],
] as [string, string | null][]).filter((r): r is [string, string] => !!r[1]) : [];
const formsBase = `/c/${clinic.slug}/patients/forms/`;
const moreItems = (money ? 1 : 0) + (canEdit ? 7 : 0);
const recHere = here;
---

<ClinicLayout groupId={clinic.group_id} clinic={{ slug: clinic.slug, name: clinic.name, area: me.area }} title={titleName} section="patient" staff={{ name: session.name, role: session.role }} branches={branches} finance={clinic.can_view_finance} layout="panes" heading>
  {/* The patient's name is the page's title, in the top bar (the layout's heading), as on a
      person's page and a statement: this card is who they are beside it — the avatar, the few
      facts, the actions and the four numbers — with no second name. */}
  <Pane as="div" label={`${shortName}, patient record`}>
    <a href={`/c/${clinic.slug}/patients/`} class="rec-back" data-pts-back><Icon name="chevron-left" />Back to patients</a>
    <script>
      // Back to the list as it was left: the same search, filter and sort (./_list/back.ts).
      import { restoreBackLinks } from './_list/back';
      restoreBackLinks();
    </script>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-4">
      <div class="rec-who">
        <Avatar name={shortName} size="lg" />
        <p class="rec-facts min-w-0"><span class="rec-facts-in"><span><span class="pt-ref" title="Chart no."><span class="sr-only">Chart no. </span>{patient.chart_no}</span></span>{facts.map((f) => <span>{f}</span>)}</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="rec-actions">
        <a href={bookHref} class="ws-btn ws-btn-primary md:order-last"><Icon name="calendar" />New booking</a>
        {canEdit && <button type="button" class="ws-btn ws-btn-quiet" data-ws-open="details"><Icon name="user" />Edit details</button>}
        {moreItems > 0 && (
          <Menu id="rec-more" label={`More for ${shortName}`} buttonClass="ws-btn ws-btn-quiet" align="right">
            <Fragment slot="button">More <Icon name="chevron" size={16} /></Fragment>
            {canEdit && (
              <>
                <button type="button" class="ws-menu-item" data-ws-open="rec-note-add" data-amends="" data-rec-show="notes">
                  <span class="ws-menu-icon" data-tint="blue"><Glyph name="pen" /></span>
                  <span class="ws-menu-words">Clinical note<span class="ws-menu-hint">What was found and done today</span></span>
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="ws-menu-item" data-ws-open="rec-plan-add" data-rec-show="treatment">
                  <span class="ws-menu-icon" data-tint="green"><Glyph name="plan" /></span>
                  <span class="ws-menu-words">Add to treatment plan<span class="ws-menu-hint">With the price from your fee guide</span></span>
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="ws-menu-item" data-ws-open="rec-rx-add" data-rec-show="rx">
                  <span class="ws-menu-icon" data-tint="blue"><Glyph name="pill" /></span>
                  <span class="ws-menu-words">Prescription<span class="ws-menu-hint">Ready to print, with PRC and PTR</span></span>
                </button>
